#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_settings.rst:144
msgid ""
"**A version of Python Interpreter**. :ref:`piocore` is written in `Python "
"language <https://www.python.org/>`__, including development :ref:"
"`platforms`. We need to know which Python version produces such type of "
"exceptions (see below), which is more popular, which version we should drop "
"and focus on a new one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_settings.rst:148
msgid ""
":ref:`piocore` **errors/exceptions**. We report automatically fatal "
"exceptions raised by `PlatformIO Core source code <https://github.com/"
"platformio/platformio-core>`__ but NOT by your project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_settings.rst:150
msgid ""
"**The name of the used platform, board, framework**. We collect this type of "
"information to have a clear picture which software products are the most "
"widely used by our Community and for the which we should provide frequent "
"updates and add new features ( for example, \"atmelavr\", \"arduino\", "
"\"uno\", etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_settings.rst:154
msgid ""
"**The name of CLI command**. It helps us to improve our CLI. For example, "
"\"run\", \"lib list\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_settings.rst:156
msgid ""
"The name of :ref:`ide`. This is very important information for us. We create "
"native extensions based on the popularity of IDEs (for example, :ref:"
"`ide_vscode`, :ref:`ide_clion`)"
msgstr ""

